From a9eecedc34ac1e8795dd45ef2b7e73f11165abf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 19:33:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: View List band labels white, not crimson

The .band_block recolor forced crimson text, but in the index.asp View List
the band label (5G-1/LINK) renders directly on the blue interface chip -
unreadable. White matches the stock RT treatment there; the network-map
variant keeps its own black-on-cyan span rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
index a338ce5a18..289dc5f798 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
+++ b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ div[id$="_Block_PC"] div:hover,#ClientList_Block a:hover,#WDSAPList div:hover,
 .bandtext{color:#B7B1A4!important}
 .conn_status_hint>a{color:#E0A93B!important}
 .blue_line{background-color:#E10600!important;border-color:#E10600!important}
-.band_block{border-color:#E10600!important;color:#E10600!important}
+.band_block{border-color:#E10600!important;color:#FFF!important} /* label sits on the blue chip in View List - crimson was unreadable */
 .division-block{border-left-color:#E10600!important}
 .guestNetwork_name_edited,.gnset_edit_titleName{color:#ECE7DB!important}
 .gnset_copySettingContent_txt{color:#E0A93B!important}
